{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Like a bundle of stone</b> — it is not fitting for preciousness, for it is not described with preciousness." "<b>And in margamah</b> — a praiseworthy thing, and its cognate is argaman (purple), and likewise ragmatam, whose meaning is tifartam (their splendor). And so the interpretation of כצרור is: just as a person binds a fine stone in a margamah within a bundle, so one gives honor to a fool. He likens the bundle to the giver, and the stone to the fool, and the margamah to the honor."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:24:50.446798991Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}